{"id": "EUVD-2026-80645", "enisaUuid": "d417d78d-62a7-3362-b845-b8308d22fe75", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during close_lru reaping\n\nAn nfs4_openowner left on nn->close_lru after its final CLOSE keeps\nits last closed stateid in oo_last_closed_stid, holding only a raw\npointer to its nfs4_client. The laundromat reaps timed-out entries,\ndrops nn->client_lock, and calls nfs4_put_stid(), which dereferences\nthe client through cl_lock. Nothing pins the client across that\nwindow, so a concurrent force_expire_client() can free it and\nnfs4_put_stid() reads freed memory. __destroy_client() hits the same\nrace, walking clp->cl_openowners without cl_lock.\n\nPin the client with cl_rpc_users before dropping client_lock, and\nskip clients already expiring. __destroy_client() then cleans up its\nown close_lru entries through release_last_closed_stateid(), so\nteardown no longer races the laundromat.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:33", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/adc34b5df5c5d87043cb500b0867fc1c4ad0117e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0763482227822f7343557f086afc382086d56c4c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83dd59ac1c3455c2c7d8ddb582d980a13199b9b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e57a9ed34ea8c17e831de59b8f1a6b2d80d347a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2330b788d732f43668b965b3105b37ceb276dfea"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cj69-89jw-ggxp", "CVE-2026-90037"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e691039-1308-32e2-9f78-fa194d161986", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "13577206-f148-3b7d-91ce-39584279232c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "217526e7ecc9f6f243e976772e81eab7ab986a4c <2330b788d732f43668b965b3105b37ceb276dfea"}, {"id": "5e1f849d-b6d4-3f31-b674-4f33723442bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "217526e7ecc9f6f243e976772e81eab7ab986a4c <e57a9ed34ea8c17e831de59b8f1a6b2d80d347a1"}, {"id": "624851b1-202f-32ca-a4a6-d7fa490ad62a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.17"}, {"id": "63b3913c-d216-30d3-9e00-453581c73bae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "217526e7ecc9f6f243e976772e81eab7ab986a4c <0763482227822f7343557f086afc382086d56c4c"}, {"id": "73585bbd-7031-3d12-a809-8fbc7b47205b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "217526e7ecc9f6f243e976772e81eab7ab986a4c <adc34b5df5c5d87043cb500b0867fc1c4ad0117e"}, {"id": "7a1d485c-0edd-39ca-9eb6-596d98a7a829", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "81630bb1-22d4-3d8e-82ee-6c4d38aeb955", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8c12b04d-aaf3-30c4-9fa7-85e3ae7f9efd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "a5480734-ad68-359a-aff1-509bd70f3610", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e48a1a6a-ff44-37a7-9d2b-b83e900e53d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "217526e7ecc9f6f243e976772e81eab7ab986a4c <83dd59ac1c3455c2c7d8ddb582d980a13199b9b3"}, {"id": "ea086f1d-c21b-36b1-a0ec-024c8d09d578", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "28f1d9ba-b7f7-3899-8587-f884edab11c6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}